version=1 id=b0000003-0003-0003-0003-000000000003

@prompt
Each line holds at most one probe: adding a probe to a line removes any probe already on it. (Different lines keep their own.) You remove a probe the same way you add it.

# Tasks
1. On the first line, probe `weekly`, then `125`, then the first `*`, then the second `*` (caret on each, **Cmd/Ctrl+E**). Each new probe replaces the one before; the green underline marks the probed expression.
2. You now have a probe on the second `*`. Remove it the same way: caret on it and **Cmd/Ctrl+E** again (or click its sample and press the same keys).

@hint
Caret on an expression, then Cmd/Ctrl+E. The same key removes a probe you already placed.

@code
let weekly = 2 * 125 * 7 in
weekly + 50
